```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor U as Usuario
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant API as FastAPI
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Q as Redis/Celery
    participant GPU as Worker GPU
    participant AI as Colorization Engine
    participant FS as Storage

    U->>FE: Edita identidad, atributos y paleta
    FE->>API: PATCH/PUT configuración
    API->>DB: Persistir cambios
    U->>FE: Aprobar configuración
    FE->>API: POST /analysis/{id}/approve
    API->>DB: Validar personajes y configuración
    API->>DB: Marcar análisis como APPROVED
    U->>FE: Solicitar colorización
    FE->>API: POST /colorizations
    API->>DB: Validar aprobación y crear job
    API->>Q: Encolar job
    API-->>FE: 202 Accepted + job_id
    Q->>GPU: Ejecutar colorización
    GPU->>FS: Leer original, máscaras y referencias
    GPU->>AI: Inferencia condicionada
    AI-->>GPU: Imagen generada
    GPU->>FS: Guardar resultado
    GPU->>DB: Marcar job COMPLETED
    FE-->>U: Mostrar resultado
```

**Source:** arc42.md §6.3 Secuencia: aprobación y colorización

**Purpose:** Shows the human-in-the-loop colorization flow: the user edits identity, attributes, and palette; the API persists changes; the user approves the configuration via POST /analysis/{id}/approve; the API validates and marks the analysis APPROVED; the user requests colorization via POST /colorizations; the API validates approval, creates a job, enqueues it, and returns 202 Accepted with job_id. The GPU worker reads the original, masks, and references, runs conditioned inference through the AI engine, stores the result, and marks the job COMPLETED.
